---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About The Small Print">
  <style>
    .nav-top { border-bottom: 1px solid #c8c3ba; padding: 0 2rem; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; height: 44px; background: #f8f6f1; }
    .nav-top a { font-size: 11px; color: #8a94a0; text-decoration: none; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
    .nav-top a:hover { color: #0d7377; }
    .nav-lang { color: #0d7377 !important; border: 0.5px solid #0d7377; padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 20px; }
    .masthead { padding: 1.5rem 2rem 1rem; text-align: center; border-bottom: 3px solid #1e2d3d; }
    .masthead-name { font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: 42px; color: #1e2d3d; letter-spacing: -0.5px; line-height: 1; }
    .masthead-name span { color: #14919B; }
    .masthead-sub { font-size: 11px; color: #8a94a0; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-top: 6px; }
    .nav-sections { display: flex; justify-content: center; border-bottom: 1px solid #c8c3ba; }
    .nav-section { font-size: 12px; padding: 10px 20px; color: #5a6472; text-decoration: none; letter-spacing: 0.04em; border-bottom: 2px solid transparent; }
    .nav-section.active { color: #1e2d3d; border-bottom: 2px solid #1e2d3d; font-weight: 500; }
    .nav-section:hover { color: #0d7377; }
    .page-body { max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 2rem; }
    .opening-line { font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: 28px; color: #1e2d3d; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 2rem; font-weight: normal; }
    .prose { font-size: 16px; color: #5a6472; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    .prose strong { color: #1e2d3d; font-weight: 500; }
    .divider { height: 1px; background: #e8e4db; margin: 2rem 0; }
    .section-label { font-size: 11px; color: #8a94a0; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .tsp-box { border-left: 2px solid #0d7377; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; background: #fff; margin: 2rem 0; }
    .tsp-box-label { font-size: 10px; color: #0d7377; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    .tsp-box-text { font-size: 15px; color: #5a6472; line-height: 1.7; }
    .structure-item { display: flex; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; align-items: flex-start; }
    .structure-number { font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: 20px; color: #c8c3ba; flex-shrink: 0; width: 24px; line-height: 1.4; }
    .structure-text { font-size: 15px; color: #5a6472; line-height: 1.6; }
    .structure-text strong { color: #1e2d3d; font-weight: 500; display: block; margin-bottom: 2px; }
    .footer { padding: 1.5rem 2rem; border-top: 1px solid #c8c3ba; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; }
    .footer-logo { font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: 16px; color: #1e2d3d; }
    .footer-logo span { color: #14919B; }
    .footer-links a { font-size: 11px; color: #8a94a0; text-decoration: none; margin-left: 16px; }
    .footer-note { font-size: 11px; color: #8a94a0; }

    @media (max-width: 720px) {
      .masthead { padding: 1rem 1.25rem 0.75rem; }
      .masthead-name { font-size: 30px; }
      .masthead-sub { font-size: 10px; }
      .nav-top { height: auto; padding: 0.6rem 1.25rem; overflow-x: auto; justify-content: flex-start; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; }
      .nav-top a { font-size: 10px; }
      .nav-top > div { flex-wrap: nowrap; gap: 14px; flex-shrink: 0; white-space: nowrap; }
      .nav-lang { flex-shrink: 0; white-space: nowrap; margin-left: 14px; }
      .nav-sections { overflow-x: auto; justify-content: flex-start; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; mask-image: linear-gradient(to right, black 88%, transparent 100%); -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(to right, black 88%, transparent 100%); }
      .nav-section { white-space: nowrap; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 11px; padding: 8px 14px; }
      .footer { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; padding: 1.25rem; }
      .footer-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 14px; }
      .footer-links a { margin-left: 0; }
    }
  </style>

  <div class="nav-top">
    <div style="display:flex; gap:20px;">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <a href="/about-tsp">About this publication</a>
      <a href="/about">Meet the author</a>
    </div>
    <a href="/es/acerca-de" class="nav-lang">En español</a>
  </div>

  <div class="masthead">
    <div class="masthead-name">The Small <span>Print</span></div>
    <div class="masthead-sub">From the study to you</div>
  </div>

  <div class="nav-sections">
    <a href="/" class="nav-section">All articles</a>
    <a href="/about-tsp" class="nav-section active">About The Small Print</a>
    <a href="/about" class="nav-section">Meet the author</a>
    <a href="/#tsp-section" class="nav-section">The Small Print §</a>
  </div>

  <div class="page-body">

    <div class="opening-line">
      For everyone who never had to read a methods section.
    </div>

    <p class="prose">
      Most of us don't read scientific papers, and not because we're not curious. It's because they weren't written for us. They were written for other scientists, reviewed by other scientists, and published in journals that most people can't access, in language that takes years to learn to decode.
    </p>

    <p class="prose">
      But the science inside those papers belongs to everyone. Much of it was funded by public money, and much of it is directly relevant to how we understand our bodies, our health, and the world around us. Yet most of it never makes it out of the journal in one piece.
    </p>

    <p class="prose">
      What usually happens instead is simple: a press release gets written, a journalist picks it up, and a headline gets published. However, something important gets lost at every step, not because anyone is being dishonest, but because the format doesn't leave room for nuance. <strong>A headline can't hold a confidence interval.</strong>
    </p>

    <div class="tsp-box">
      <div class="tsp-box-label">So, what is The Small Print?</div>
      <div class="tsp-box-text">A bilingual publication that takes real scientific studies in medicine, biomedicine, and AI, and translates them honestly for curious readers like you! Not simplified, not sensationalized, just made readable, with all the important caveats intact.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="divider"></div>

    <div class="section-label">How each article is structured</div>

    <div class="structure-item">
      <div class="structure-number">1</div>
      <div class="structure-text"><strong>What the study found</strong>The actual findings: what the researchers did, and what they saw.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="structure-item">
      <div class="structure-number">2</div>
      <div class="structure-text"><strong>Why it matters</strong>Context. Why this question was worth asking in the first place.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="structure-item">
      <div class="structure-number">3</div>
      <div class="structure-text"><strong>What it doesn't prove</strong>The part most coverage skips. What can't we conclude from this? What would we need to know more?</div>
    </div>
    <div class="structure-item">
      <div class="structure-number">4</div>
      <div class="structure-text"><strong>Important limitations</strong>Sample size, study design, conflicts of interest: the fine print of the fine print.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="structure-item">
      <div class="structure-number">5</div>
      <div class="structure-text"><strong>Real-world context</strong>What does this actually mean for people outside the lab?</div>
    </div>
    <div class="structure-item">
      <div class="structure-number">6</div>
      <div class="structure-text"><strong>The Small Print §</strong>The section that gives this publication its name. The nuances, the honest interpretation, and what the headlines will probably get wrong.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="divider"></div>

    <p class="prose">
      Every article links to the original paper, every article is published in English and Spanish, and every article is written by someone who has spent years inside the scientific process and thinks you deserve to know what that actually looks like.
    </p>

    <p class="prose"><em>A scientific publication for general readers, designed with the editorial experience of a scientific journal.</em></p>

  </div>

  <div class="footer">
    <div class="footer-logo">The Small <span>Print</span></div>
    <div class="footer-links">
      <a href="/about-tsp">About</a>
      <a href="/about">Author</a>
      <a href="mailto:dianachj@thesmallprint.pub">Contact</a>
      <a href="/es/acerca-de">En español</a>
    </div>
    <div class="footer-note">Independent · Bilingual · Freiburg</div>
  </div>
</Layout>